    3. Place 3-4 black blobs. For each, pick a random connected region (rectangle or irregular shape) of 4-55 cells, ensuring no border touching and blobs don't merge.
    4. Verify coverage constraint -- every tile phase (r%th, c%tw) has at least one non-black cell remaining. If not, shrink the largest blob or retry placement.
    5. Input = output with black-blob cells set to 0.
